### `Android BLE classes written from memory do not compile`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| `Unresolved reference` on advertise/GATT classes after writing radio Kotlin in one pass | Framework class names were guessed from plausible names: `AdvertisingSet*` (not `AdvertiseSet*`), legacy `startAdvertising` takes `(settings, data, scanResponse, callback)`, `setLegacy` is SystemApi-only, p2p manager comes from `getSystemService(WIFI_P2P_SERVICE)` (no public `getInstance`) | Write one radio subsystem, then build — do not batch five. When the error names a class, check the real signature in the Android SDK docs instead of renaming blindly |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-10 -->

### `GATT fallback link dies after the first frame`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| Every write returns `GATT_INVALID_ATTRIBUTE_LENGTH` / link silent after connect | Client chunked at a size above the effective payload: default ATT MTU is 23 → 20 usable bytes | `requestMtu(247)` after service discovery, track it in `onMtuChanged`, chunk at `mtu - 3` with a 20-byte floor. Cap reassembled frame length (e.g. 64 KB) and drop the peer buffer on overflow — a hostile length prefix must not crash the binder callback |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-10 -->

### `Live personal PSK read is always empty`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| A scripted `wpa-psk:secret` fixture passes, but a real connected personal network returns null | Terse list rows are colon-joined and escape `:` as `\:` and `\` as `\\`. A multi-field connection show is one `property:value` line, so the first line's left side is the property name, not the security mode | Split on unescaped colons, unescape, then match the `.key-mgmt` and `.psk` suffixes. A missing tool, enterprise mode, or empty secret returns null. Do not throw, and do not log that stdout |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-10 -->

### `GATT lookup fails on a fresh scan handle`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| Connect throws that the characteristic is missing immediately after a scan | The scan path has no GATT children until the device is connected and its services are resolved | Connect first (already-connected counts as success), wait until services are resolved, then look up the characteristic under that device path |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-10 -->

### `Server control writes never reach the session`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| The peripheral accepts writes, but no inbound link appears, or a second frame in the same chunk waits forever | Frames were pushed onto a broadcast stream with no listener, and one write can hold more than one length-prefixed frame | Take the peer from the write options, emit one inbound link per peer, and drain until a frame is incomplete. Drop the peer buffer on a hostile length |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-10 -->

### `Next advertisement fails because the object is already exported`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| A failed advertisement registration makes every later start fail with the object already registered | The object was exported locally, the remote register then threw, and stop returned immediately because it had no handle | Unregister the local object on that failure and again on stop |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-10 -->

### `Host chain misses a typed private-network failure`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| Hotspot or Wi-Fi Direct failure surfaces as a platform exception instead of the typed port error | The native reply used the channel error path | Reply a success map whose error field names the failure. Map that field to the typed port error. Reserve the channel error path for a missing window or a truly unknown method |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-10 -->

### `Apple scan never matches the Android advert`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| A 31-byte manufacturer payload is invisible to a CoreBluetooth scan, or the hit is two bytes long | Android's manufacturer getter strips the company id. CoreBluetooth keeps it, little-endian, in front of the payload | Advertise `D9 FD` then the 31 bytes for company id `0xFDA9`. On scan, require those two bytes and pass the rest through. Do not shorten the packed advert |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-10 -->

### `iPhone advert is invisible to a manufacturer scan`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| Android or Mac sees no iPhone, while the iPhone sees those peers | iOS advertising accepts only a local name and service UUIDs. Manufacturer data is not in the packet | Advertise the service UUID and a short local name. Serve the 31-byte payload as a GATT read. Do not shorten the shared advert, and do not invent a payload from a service UUID |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-10 -->

### `Both sides wait for the other to host`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| Two devices sit in the remote-host wait, and an all-fail never ends | Each chain lists the peer first, or a failure frame returns as success so the next owned step never speaks. A timeout also presents the next invite and sends nothing | Do not reorder the chain. Send a sealed secret after accept, or a failure frame. A failure frame continues the chain. Return only after a secret or after every remaining step has spoken. If the secret was not sent, stop that radio before the next step. The accept-owned loop does this too. Timeout sends the same failure frames as a decline. The invitee runs the steps it owns when it accepts |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-10 -->

### `Fallthrough awaits a consent prompt`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| A missing LAN password never starts the private network | The fallthrough awaited a consent read that throws when no dialog is showing | Keep the passphrase prompt on the password decision. A throw there must not sit on the fallthrough |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-10 -->

### `One control frame hides the invite`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| A hello arrives and the invite behind it never queues, or the next waiter never appears | The reader took one frame and stopped, or decline/timeout did not present the promoted invite | Drain the link. Hello only installs keys. Present again when a waiter is promoted |

