### `Idle stop leaves the session hosting`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| Idle fires, the radio stops, and the next check still thinks a network is up. A joiner stays on the peer network. Or a live transfer is torn down because the client count was never written | Stop calls were not the disband path, teardown never left the joined network, or in-use counts were stale | Use the same teardown as disband: clear hosted state and leave the joined network. Refresh transfer and client counts before idle or shutdown. A join or a delivered secret counts as a client |

